          "title": "Gile",
          "subtitle": "Trick-taking",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Gile, also called Cuarenta y una, is an Envite-family point-trick game using a Spanish pack and discarding."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Gile is a Spanish-pack point-trick game of the Envite family. It is played as a four-hand game, with a five-player form also recorded, and uses a shortened Spanish pack."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "4, also 5 players use the table arrangement described for Gile."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "28-card Spanish pack"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "28-card Spanish pack, score area, and enough table space for play."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Deal 28-card Spanish pack for 4, also 5 players according to the local rules before the first trick."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
